    {
      "id": "F-002",
      "severity": "medium",
      "summary": "The progress-rule module docstring incorrectly says an unreadable worktree counts as progress and prevents the rule from stopping the lane.",
      "evidence": [
        "scripts/task_run/task_run_progress_rule.py says an unobservable worktree counts as progress, so the rule never stops a lane it cannot see.",
        "In on_tick, an unreadable fingerprint makes tree_changed false; without another outcome, the window has no progress. The selected test test_an_unobservable_worktree_falls_back_to_the_executors_own_events confirms silence can still lead to a request and stop."
      ],
      "action": "Correct the docstring: an unreadable worktree prevents loop claims but does not count as progress for window checks."
    }
  ],
